213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 117 0 R
/T (For decades, we have demanded restitution, called for reparation, named the violence of erasure, and insisted on the return of what was taken. This insistence has been necessary. It has been dignified. It has been just.)
/E (For decades, we have demanded restitution, called for reparation, named the violence of erasure, and insisted on the return of what was taken. This insistence has been necessary. It has been dignified. It has been just.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 117 0 R
/T (And yet in the midst of it all, we must ask: at what cost does a struggle remain outward-facing? How long can we organize our becoming around the recognition of former powers?)
/E (And yet in the midst of it all, we must ask: at what cost does a struggle remain outward-facing? How long can we organize our becoming around the recognition of former powers?)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
