228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 118 0 R
/T (Frantz Fanon reminds us in his 1961 book, The Wretched of the Earth, that each generation must discover its mission. Perhaps ours is no longer only to retrieve fragments of the past, but to remember that the source from which they emerged is inexhaustible.)
/E (Frantz Fanon reminds us in his 1961 book, The Wretched of the Earth, that each generation must discover its mission. Perhaps ours is no longer only to retrieve fragments of the past, but to remember that the source from which they emerged is inexhaustible.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
