/P 119 0 R
/T (The power was never contained in the things lost. It lived, and still very much lives, in our cosmologies, languages and land-based knowledge systems. It lives in our rituals, in our rhythm and in memory-keeping traditions that cannot be looted. What was taken were just expressions of who we are, but what remains is origin.)
/E (The power was never contained in the things lost. It lived, and still very much lives, in our cosmologies, languages and land-based knowledge systems. It lives in our rituals, in our rhythm and in memory-keeping traditions that cannot be looted. What was taken were just expressions of who we are, but what remains is origin.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
