249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 120 0 R
/T (Pan-African thought has always understood circularity. That the river does not argue for its existence but flows and that seeds do not petition the soil but root. So also, regeneration cannot be negotiated but enacted.)
/E (Pan-African thought has always understood circularity. That the river does not argue for its existence but flows and that seeds do not petition the soil but root. So also, regeneration cannot be negotiated but enacted.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 120 0 R
/T (Reindigenization proposes a similar movement. It is cyclical and reorders imagination around renewal rather than grievance. It turns inward and downward - toward soil, toward memory systems that survived erasure, toward cosmologies that were never fully extractable. It restores reciprocity between culture and ecology - language and land, ritual and season, body and territory. It is creation without permission. Culture enacted so fully that validation becomes peripheral.)
/E (Reindigenization proposes a similar movement. It is cyclical and reorders imagination around renewal rather than grievance. It turns inward and downward - toward soil, toward memory systems that survived erasure, toward cosmologies that were never fully extractable. It restores reciprocity between culture and ecology - language and land, ritual and season, body and territory. It is creation without permission. Culture enacted so fully that validation becomes peripheral.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
