/Title (This biennial makes space for an honest, courageous dialogue about the ways we may have over-identified with victimhood, how we cling to our wounds so tightly that we forget our capacity to heal. It seeks to propose practical ways, not just thoughts, of how we can channel our energies towards re-indigenizing our spaces, practices and rhythms.)
