/Title (Frantz Fanon reminds us in his 1961 book, The Wretched of the Earth, that each generation must discover its mission. Perhaps ours is no longer only to retrieve fragments of the past, but to remember that the source from which they emerged is inexhaustible.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 822 0 R
/Prev 932 0 R
>>
endobj
912 0 obj
<<
/Title (The power was never contained in the things lost. It lived, and still very much lives, in our cosmologies, languages and land-based knowledge systems. It lives in our rituals, in our rhythm and in memory-keeping traditions that cannot be looted. What was taken were just expressions of who we are, but what remains is origin.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 678 0 R
/Prev 823 0 R
/Next 933 0 R
>>
endobj
913 0 obj
<<
/Title (Chasing is exhausting. It narrows the horizon to a single point - the thing taken, the thing withheld, the thing owed. It convinces us that wholeness lies elsewhere. It fixes our gaze on the hand that removed, rather than the hand that still creates.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 678 0 R
/Prev 933 0 R
/Next 824 0 R
>>
endobj
